Fixes reindex failures with the Symfony Redis cache on phpredis (Magento 2.4.9, on top of AC-17650):
"RedisTagAdapter::getTagKey(): Argument #1 ($tag) must be of type string, false given",
"Array sizes are inconsistent" and "Unable to unserialize value" in indexers that run after the first failure.

Root cause 1: with phpredis the pipeline is not a separate object but a mode of the shared \Redis connection
(the same connection is used by Symfony's RedisAdapter and by every cache frontend on the same host/db).
An exception thrown while commands are queued (e.g. the getTagKey() TypeError in onRemove) leaves the
connection in PIPELINE mode, so every later command in the process gets the wrong reply.
Fix: queueing loops are wrapped in try/catch that discards the pipeline before rethrowing, and
createPipeline()/onRemove() bring a connection left in PIPELINE/MULTI mode back to ATOMIC mode.

Root cause 2: once the reply stream is out of sync, SCARD returns a different number of replies than
commands sent and SMEMBERS returns nil-derived false values instead of tag names.
Fix: getIdsMatchingTags(), onRemove() and pruneTagIndexPipelined() detect misaligned replies and
re-open the phpredis connection in place (same host, port, timeouts, persistent id, auth, db), then retry.

Predis is not affected (its pipeline is a separate object), which is why environments without the
redis PHP extension do not reproduce the issue.

